  "notes": "Piece 2 of the sign-up plan, the library's part, on top of feat/sign-up-the-switch-and-the-log-in-line (piece 1, published first). POST /user/signup without an invite asks an email and a password and makes the account with an empty name (a blank one gets the log-in route's sentence, now user-server BlankCredentials.REFUSAL); a request already signed in makes nothing and keeps its session; a welcome mail that cannot be sent no longer fails the sign-up. user-ui: the form without an invite is Email, Password, the product's sentence above Sign up (AuthPageProduct.signupAgreementSentence, optional) and Have an account? Log in (AuthQuietLink, the quiet lines' one style); the invite form is unchanged. The sign-up check and the founder's list (piece 3) continue on this branch. Held: nothing landed or published."
